---
layout: base.njk
---
{% set s = schedule %}
{% macro chip(r) %}{% set tip %}{{ r.id }}: {{ r.task }} ({{ r.stateLabel }}{% if r.note %}; {{ r.note }}{% endif %}){% endset %}{% if r.href %}<a class="chip chip-{{ r.state }}" href="{{ r.href }}" title="{{ tip }}">{{ r.study }}</a>{% else %}<span class="chip chip-{{ r.state }}" title="{{ tip }}">{{ r.study }}</span>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro line(r) %}<li><span class="chip chip-{{ r.state }}">{{ r.stateLabel }}</span> <strong>{{ r.id }}</strong>, {{ r.earliest }}{% if r.latest %} to {{ r.latest }}{% else %} onwards{% endif %}: {{ r.task }}{% if r.note %} <span class="sched-note">{{ r.note }}</span>{% endif %}{% if r.ref %} <span class="sched-note">({{ r.ref }})</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endmacro %}
<article class="index schedule">
  <h1>Schedule</h1>
  {% if not s %}<p>No schedule yet.</p>{% else %}
  <p class="lede">Everything Lighthouse has promised to do, from its reads to its write-ups, each with a window and a status. Scheduled agent runs take what is due; a run that never happens leaves a row overdue here, not a hole in the record. As of {{ s.today }}, the date of this page's last build; the table is <a href="https://github.com/JKershaw/lighthouse/blob/main/schedule/due.csv">schedule/due.csv</a> and a run follows <a href="/schedule/runner/">its instructions</a>.</p>

  <ul class="sched-counts">{% for c in s.counts %}<li><span class="chip chip-{{ c.state }}">{{ c.label }}</span> {{ c.n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

  {% if s.attention.length %}<h2>Needs attention</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.attention %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.due.length %}<h2>Due now</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.due %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  <h2>The coming weeks</h2>
  <p class="sched-note">Each study appears on the day its window opens; hover or tap for the task. Rows without an end date are listed below.</p>
  <div class="sched-cal" role="table" aria-label="Scheduled rows by the day their window opens, {{ s.range.first }} to {{ s.range.last }}">
    <div class="sched-row sched-head" role="row">{% for d in ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"] %}<div role="columnheader">{{ d }}</div>{% endfor %}</div>
    {% for w in s.weeks %}<div class="sched-row" role="row">
      {% for d in w.days %}<div role="cell" class="sched-day{% if d.isToday %} is-today{% endif %}{% if d.isPast %} is-past{% endif %}{% if not d.items.length %} is-empty{% endif %}">
        <span class="sched-date">{{ d.day }}{% if d.day == 1 or loop.first %}<span class="sched-month">/{{ d.month }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {% for r in d.items %}{{ chip(r) }}{% endfor %}
      </div>{% endfor %}
    </div>{% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if s.openEnded.length %}<h2>Open-ended</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.openEnded %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.beyond.length %}<h2>Further ahead</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.beyond %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.recent.length %}<h2>Recently done or missed</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.recent %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</article>
